  <BaseGameText>

    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_NAME">
      <Text>Heaven-Sent Swallow</Text>
    </Row>
    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_DESC">
      <Text>All your cities gain +1 Amenity. Cities with a Holy Site gain a further +1 Food, +2 Faith, +1 Culture, +2 Housing and +1 Amenity. Your capital gains +1 Faith, +2 Food, +2 Production and +3 Gold per turn, and Holy Sites are built 50% faster. Each Farm adjacent to a Holy Site gives that Holy Site +1 Faith. Production is not granted directly - it comes from Diligence converting Holy Site adjacency. Also grants Cleaving Thorns, Four Rivers, Diligence, Enduring Pioneers, The Maker's Name, Imperial Highway and Unified Statutes. Imperial Scale (from the Classical era onward; the Ancient era is fully exempt): all cities suffer -10% Science, cities of 10 or more population suffer -12% more (-22% in total), and cities of 16 or more suffer a further -8% (-30% in total) - so Science no longer scales linearly with population; the larger the city, the heavier the drag.</Text>
    </Row>

    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_MR_NAME">
      <Text>Cleaving Thorns</Text>
    </Row>
    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_MR_DESC">
      <Text>Tundra tiles provide +1 Faith and +1 Production. Farms may be built on Tundra, and on Tundra Hills once Civil Engineering is unlocked. On Tundra, Tundra Hills, Snow and Snow Hills, Farms and Camps provide +2 Food, Mines and Lumber Mills provide +2 Production, strategic resource accumulation is +100%, and tile purchase cost is 50% lower. Newly founded cities claim 5 extra tiles of territory.</Text>
    </Row>

    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_MK_NAME">
      <Text>Four Rivers</Text>
    </Row>
    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_MK_DESC">
      <Text>Holy Sites receive a major adjacency bonus from Rivers, yield Food equal to their adjacency bonus, gain +2 Housing when adjacent to a River, and trigger a Culture Bomb when built.</Text>
    </Row>

    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_BEL_NAME">
      <Text>Diligence</Text>
    </Row>
    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_BEL_DESC">
      <Text>Grants Dance of the Aurora (+1 Faith to Holy Sites per adjacent Tundra tile), Work Ethic (Holy Site adjacency becomes Production), Jesuit Education (buy Campus and Theater buildings with Faith) and the Scripture policy effect (+50% Holy Site adjacency). Dance of the Aurora works immediately and needs no Pantheon; Work Ethic and Jesuit Education require a founded religion that your cities follow.</Text>
    </Row>

    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_MOVE_NAME">
      <Text>Enduring Pioneers</Text>
    </Row>
    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_MOVE_DESC">
      <Text>Scouts +3 Movement (3 to 6), Settlers +2 Movement (2 to 4).</Text>
    </Row>

    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_BUILDER_NAME">
      <Text>The Maker's Name</Text>
    </Row>
    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_BUILDER_DESC">
      <Text>Builders may expend a charge to add 30% progress to any Wonder under construction. From the Renaissance era onward, this falls to 15%.</Text>
    </Row>

    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_ROAD_NAME">
      <Text>Imperial Highway</Text>
    </Row>
    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_ROAD_DESC">
      <Text>Every city you found is immediately connected to your capital by road.</Text>
    </Row>

    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_EDICT_NAME">
      <Text>Unified Statutes</Text>
    </Row>
    <Row Tag="LOC_TRAIT_NHS_EDICT_DESC">
      <Text>You gain 1 extra Wildcard policy slot from the start of the game, in every government.</Text>
    </Row>

